1
00:00:00,560 --> 00:00:01,000
Friday.

2
00:00:01,600 --> 00:00:02,040
Nine A.M.

3
00:00:02,860 --> 00:00:05,480
An AI agent has the keys to a marketplace's

4
00:00:05,540 --> 00:00:06,340
PayPal account.

5
00:00:07,020 --> 00:00:09,320
It's about to send fifteen hundred dollars...

6
00:00:10,020 --> 00:00:11,560
and four hundred and fourteen of it...

7
00:00:11,980 --> 00:00:13,000
is UNDER DISPUTE.

8
00:00:13,460 --> 00:00:15,780
AI agents can now refund buyers...

9
00:00:16,200 --> 00:00:17,140
accept disputes...

10
00:00:17,560 --> 00:00:18,720
and send payouts.

11
00:00:19,480 --> 00:00:22,140
Nothing in PayPal makes them ask a human first.

12
00:00:22,660 --> 00:00:24,780
And a prompt that says "please confirm"...

13
00:00:25,200 --> 00:00:26,300
is NOT a lock.

14
00:00:27,220 --> 00:00:28,640
So we built the lock.

15
00:00:29,280 --> 00:00:29,980
CounterSign.

16
00:00:30,580 --> 00:00:31,860
The AI proposes.

17
00:00:32,280 --> 00:00:33,700
The code countersigns.

18
00:00:34,927 --> 00:00:37,887
Every proposal goes through a shield of sixteen named

19
00:00:37,987 --> 00:00:38,407
rules.

20
00:00:38,826 --> 00:00:39,227
Allow.

21
00:00:39,627 --> 00:00:40,007
Block.

22
00:00:40,387 --> 00:00:41,367
Or wait for the owner.

23
00:00:41,867 --> 00:00:42,547
Only then...

24
00:00:42,827 --> 00:00:44,427
does the executor call PayPal.

25
00:00:44,920 --> 00:00:47,840
One staged week, on a PayPal mock built from

26
00:00:47,980 --> 00:00:49,420
real sandbox recordings.

27
00:00:50,180 --> 00:00:50,560
Monday.

28
00:00:51,140 --> 00:00:53,440
A buyer disputes a four hundred dollar order.

29
00:00:53,980 --> 00:00:55,240
PayPal freezes the money...

30
00:00:55,680 --> 00:00:57,880
and CounterSign holds back the maker's share.

31
00:00:58,640 --> 00:00:59,160
Thursday.

32
00:00:59,720 --> 00:01:01,500
A payout is stuck on a typo.

33
00:01:01,960 --> 00:01:03,980
The AI cancels it, on its own...

34
00:01:04,480 --> 00:01:06,200
and waits for PayPal to confirm.

35
00:01:06,913 --> 00:01:07,373
Friday.

36
00:01:07,933 --> 00:01:09,833
The naive agent pays everyone...

37
00:01:10,253 --> 00:01:11,673
disputed shares included.

38
00:01:12,493 --> 00:01:15,393
CounterSign holds back four hundred and fourteen dollars...

39
00:01:15,833 --> 00:01:18,213
and asks the owner for one exact run.

40
00:01:18,813 --> 00:01:20,693
One thousand and eighty-six dollars.

41
00:01:21,107 --> 00:01:22,247
Ten named checks.

42
00:01:22,887 --> 00:01:23,967
One payload hash.

43
00:01:24,527 --> 00:01:26,207
The owner signs it with a passkey...

44
00:01:26,667 --> 00:01:27,867
on their own device.

45
00:01:28,387 --> 00:01:31,007
A plain click can NEVER fake that signature.

46
00:01:31,527 --> 00:01:32,827
Then we cut the network...

47
00:01:33,487 --> 00:01:35,386
right after PayPal accepts the payout.

48
00:01:35,907 --> 00:01:38,487
The executor retries, with the same keys.

49
00:01:38,987 --> 00:01:41,047
PayPal points back to the original batch.

50
00:01:41,507 --> 00:01:42,307
Exactly.

51
00:01:42,867 --> 00:01:43,127
One.

52
00:01:43,627 --> 00:01:44,047
Payment.

53
00:01:44,380 --> 00:01:45,920
And it isn't just our agent.

54
00:01:46,480 --> 00:01:48,400
CounterSign is an MCP server...

55
00:01:48,780 --> 00:01:50,620
so any AI agent can plug in.

56
00:01:51,240 --> 00:01:53,960
Here, one is tricked into refunding a buyer to

57
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:55,120
a stranger's account.

58
00:01:55,680 --> 00:01:56,060
Blocked.

59
00:01:56,540 --> 00:01:57,960
Three rules, named.

60
00:01:58,400 --> 00:01:59,080
Nothing sent.

61
00:01:59,380 --> 00:02:00,800
And this is no mockup.

62
00:02:01,120 --> 00:02:02,520
This is the real build,

63
00:02:02,780 --> 00:02:04,760
on PayPal's real APIs.

64
00:02:05,220 --> 00:02:05,700
Payouts.

65
00:02:05,880 --> 00:02:06,480
Disputes.

66
00:02:06,740 --> 00:02:07,140
Orders.

67
00:02:07,360 --> 00:02:07,880
Webhooks.

68
00:02:08,280 --> 00:02:09,640
PayPal's Agent Toolkit...

69
00:02:09,940 --> 00:02:11,780
with every write tool switched off.

70
00:02:12,200 --> 00:02:13,820
Google Gemini reads the mess.

71
00:02:14,160 --> 00:02:15,180
The code decides.

72
00:02:15,580 --> 00:02:16,720
And every single run...

73
00:02:16,980 --> 00:02:19,320
is yours to slice, in AG Grid.

74
00:02:19,820 --> 00:02:22,400
The key PayPal assumptions were tested on the real

75
00:02:22,560 --> 00:02:23,520
sandbox first.

76
00:02:24,120 --> 00:02:25,060
Thirteen checks.

77
00:02:25,500 --> 00:02:27,360
Over a thousand recorded calls.

78
00:02:28,060 --> 00:02:28,800
Four were wrong...

79
00:02:29,380 --> 00:02:31,520
so the design changed to match PayPal.

80
00:02:32,480 --> 00:02:34,020
Forty-eight fault scenarios.

81
00:02:34,440 --> 00:02:35,300
Five runs each.

82
00:02:35,920 --> 00:02:37,260
Zero duplicate settlements.

83
00:02:37,760 --> 00:02:39,460
Zero refunds without the owner.

84
00:02:39,920 --> 00:02:42,200
Zero payments to an unverified payee.

85
00:02:42,787 --> 00:02:44,487
AI can move money now.

86
00:02:45,427 --> 00:02:47,367
CounterSign makes sure it asks first.

87
00:02:47,927 --> 00:02:49,127
The AI proposes.

88
00:02:49,507 --> 00:02:50,927
The code countersigns.
